FB-WIZARD-002

**Guided Wizard: Resume Upload + Application Mode Setup**

Pod 1 Feature Brief | Roadmap: P12 | Ref: VERSION_METHODOLOGY.docx

1. Problem Statement

The guided intake wizard (FB-CHAT-002) walks users through 7 steps of
search preferences but never asks them to upload a resume or choose an
application mode. Users exit the wizard with filters populated but no
resume attached and no mode selected. This means the setup gate
(AF-002) blocks them the moment they try to apply, and the AI-powered
filter onboarding promise (P12) is only partially delivered.

Two new steps at the end of the wizard close both gaps:
  - Step 8: Upload your resume
  - Step 9: Choose your application mode

2. Implementation Authority

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+
| **POD 2 MUST NOT:**                                                   |
|                                                                       |
| -   Skip the resume upload step or make it mandatory                  |
|     (it must be skippable but strongly encouraged)                    |
|                                                                       |
| -   Add mode options beyond the existing 6 from apply-workflow.js     |
|                                                                       |
| -   Call any AI endpoint from the wizard itself — resume parsing      |
|     happens via existing EFs after upload completes                   |
|                                                                       |
| -   Change the existing 7 steps or their ordering                    |
|                                                                       |
| Any deviation requires written Pod 1 approval before implementation.  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

3. Step 8: Resume Upload

3.1 UI

Conversational header: "Almost there! Upload your resume so we can
match you to the right jobs automatically."

Sub-text: "We'll extract your skills and experience to create
personalized filters. PDF or Word accepted."

Content area:
  - Drag-and-drop upload zone (reuse pattern from Resumes tab)
  - File picker button: "Choose file" (accepts .pdf, .doc, .docx)
  - 5MB file size limit
  - Upload progress indicator (spinner → green check on success)
  - After upload: show resume name + "Uploaded ✓" confirmation
  - Skip link: "Skip for now →" (bottom of step, subtle styling)

3.2 On Upload

1. Call existing addResume() flow from resumes.js:
   - Upload file to Supabase Storage
   - Create resume record
   - Extract text via extractTextFromFile()
   - Extract keywords via extractResumeKeywords()

2. Auto-create a saved filter from extracted keywords:
   - Take top 5-8 keywords from extraction
   - Create a saved filter named "From my resume" (or resume filename)
   - Populate whatPills with extracted keywords
   - If location data found in resume text, populate wherePills
   - If salary expectations found, populate payPills
   - Save via commitSaveFilter()
   - This filter becomes the user's first saved search

3. Set as active resume:
   - Mark this resume as the default for applications
   - Write activeResumeId to apply settings

3.3 On Skip

- Set a flag: bj_wizard_resume_skipped = true (localStorage)
- Proceed to Step 9
- No resume created, no auto-filter generated
- Get Started page will still show the resume upload prompt

3.4 PostHog Events

- wizard_resume_uploaded: { file_type, file_size_kb, keywords_extracted }
- wizard_resume_skipped: { step: 8 }
- wizard_auto_filter_created: { keyword_count, has_location, has_salary }

4. Step 9: Application Mode

4.1 UI

Conversational header varies based on resume upload:
  - If resume uploaded: "Great resume! Last step — how do you want to
    apply to jobs?"
  - If skipped: "One more thing — how do you want to apply to jobs?"

Sub-text: "You can change this anytime in Settings."

Content area: 6 mode cards (same visual pattern as Step 1 and Step 5
option cards). Single-select. Cards:

  1. Manual (default selected)
     Label: "I'll apply myself"
     Sub: "Review each job and apply on the company's site"
     Icon: hand

  2. Score-Gated
     Label: "Score my resume first"
     Sub: "See how well you match before applying"
     Icon: bar-chart-3

  3. Auto-Apply
     Label: "Apply automatically"
     Sub: "We submit applications for you"
     Icon: zap

  4. Auto + Score Gate
     Label: "Auto-apply if score is high"
     Sub: "Only auto-submit when your resume matches well"
     Icon: shield-check

  5. Auto Rewrite
     Label: "Rewrite + apply"
     Sub: "AI tailors your resume per job, then submits"
     Icon: wand-2

  6. Full Autopilot
     Label: "Full autopilot"
     Sub: "Rewrite and submit everything automatically"
     Icon: rocket

4.2 On Selection

- Write mode to localStorage bj_apply_settings.default_apply_mode
- Write to Supabase via syncApplySettingsToSupabase()
- If score-gated mode selected, show inline threshold slider:
  "Minimum score to apply: 75%" (range 30-95, default 75)
  Write threshold to bj_apply_settings.default_score_threshold

4.3 On Complete (Finish button)

- Same flow as current wizard completion:
  - Assemble prompt from all 9 steps
  - Call chat-job-search EF
  - Save as prompt with derived_filters
- Additionally:
  - Call checkAndSetSetupComplete() from apply-workflow.js
  - If resume uploaded + mode selected: setup_complete = true
  - User lands on job feed with filters populated, resume attached,
    mode configured — ready to apply immediately

4.4 PostHog Events

- wizard_mode_selected: { mode, has_resume }
- wizard_threshold_set: { threshold, mode }
- wizard_completed_full: { steps_completed, has_resume, mode,
    auto_filter_created, total_time_ms }

5. Changes to Existing Wizard

5.1 Step Count

- _WIZ_TOTAL: 7 → 9
- _WIZ_STEPS array: append two new entries:
  { id: 8, title: 'Resume', required: false }
  { id: 9, title: 'Apply Mode', required: false }

5.2 Progress Bar

- Progress bar segments update from 7 to 9 segments
- Width per segment: 100/9 = ~11.1%

5.3 Prompt Assembly

- Step 8 (resume) does NOT contribute to the search prompt
  (it creates a filter separately)
- Step 9 (mode) does NOT contribute to the search prompt
  (it configures apply settings separately)
- _wizAssemblePrompt() only reads steps 1-7 as before

5.4 Navigation

- Step 7 "Next" button goes to Step 8 (was "Finish")
- Step 8 "Next" goes to Step 9
- Step 9 has "Finish" button (triggers prompt assembly + completion)
- Back button from Step 8 goes to Step 7
- Back button from Step 9 goes to Step 8

